  data: {
    LLM: 'Game: Lora. Balkan compendium, 4 players, 32-card deck (A-7). 8 rounds: 1)No Tricks(-1/trick) 2)No Hearts(-1/heart) 3)No Queens(-4/queen) 4)No Kâ™¥(-8) 5)No Last Trick(-8) 6)Lora(shedding, positive) 7)Negative Lora 8)Double Negative. Deal 8 each. Must follow suit. Lowest total score wins.',
    Player: "Welcome to Lora! Over 8 rounds, you'll face different challenges: avoid winning tricks, avoid Hearts, avoid Queens, avoid the King of Hearts, avoid the last trick, then switch to shedding in The Lora rounds. Each round needs different strategyâ€”stay flexible!",
    objective: 'Score the fewest points in negative rounds and most in positive rounds.',
    gameplay: "Eight rounds played in sequence: 1. **No Tricks**: -1 pt per trick won. 2. **No Hearts**: -1 pt per Heart captured. 3. **No Queens (Jacks)**: -4 pts per Queen (or Jack) captured. 4. **No King of Hearts**: -8 pts for capturing the King of Hearts (The 'Hairy' King). 5. **No Last Trick**: -8 pts for winning the last trick. 6. **The Lora**: A shedding round. Players play cards in sequences (like Fan-Tan). First to empty their hand wins points. 7. **Negative Lora**: Inverse of round 6. 8. **Double Negative**: Points from all previous rounds combined into one super-avoidance round.",
    keyRules: [
      'Standard trick-taking: Must follow suit. No trumps (except in specific variations).',
      'Rounds 1-5, 8 are negative (avoid points).',
      'Round 6-7 are shedding games (positive scoring).',
      'Each round has specific penalty weights.',
      'Lowest cumulative score after 8 rounds wins.',
